# Git remotes (required)

Canonical detail: [docs/development/git-remotes-and-deployment.md](docs/development/git-remotes-and-deployment.md).

## Remote roles

| Remote | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `origin` (`sallen-wiley/next.js-test`) | **Working remote** — feature branches, PRs, `preview`, Vercel |
| `wiley` (`wiley/pp-ux-tooling`) | **Official publication** — `main` only |
| `rarebush` (`rarebush/ux-tooling`) | **Backup** — `main` only, no other branches |

## Working branches

- Create, push, and open PRs **only on `origin`**.
- Never push feature/working branches (or `preview`) to `wiley` or `rarebush`.

## After work lands on `main`

1. Push `main` to **all three**: `origin`, `wiley`, `rarebush`.
2. Fast-forward `preview` to `main` and push **only** to `origin` (`git branch -f preview main && git push origin preview`).
3. Verify `0	0` for `main` vs `origin/main`, `wiley/main`, `rarebush/main`, and `origin/preview`.

Do **not** stop at the tracked upstream alone.
